=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
A full four-phase sweep of the Kath4 topology finds the network operating correctly at every layer. Phase 1 reachability testing showed all 28 host-pair ping probes completing with 0% packet loss, including cross-VLAN paths that exercise both campus gateway stacks (mswitch0 serving VLANs 10/20/30; sshswitch serving VLANs 5/6). Phase A confirmed no ACL or firewall drop rules, all 15 hosts carry valid IPv4 addresses and default routes, and gateway ARP entries on VLAN 5 hosts show sshswitch's gateway (10.5.0.254) as REACHABLE. The only l2_snapshot flags were null-MAC tunnel interfaces (tunl0, sit0, gre0, etc.) in DOWN state on every host — standard Linux kernel virtual interfaces that are never active in this topology, not a MAC conflict. Phase B OSPF snapshot showed all nine routers with Full adjacencies and identical 17-route tables; mswitch0 and sshswitch both have their VLAN gateway interfaces advertised correctly into OSPF area 0. TC snapshot returned no shaped or irregular qdiscs. Phase C link/DHCP history found zero suspicious events — no carrier transitions, no lease failures, no evidence of a prior disruption. Phase D pressure sweep found no resource stress on any device. The reported symptom ("both halves of campus can't reach their gateways, started after a reload") left no traces in link history, syslog, or carrier counters. Without a flap script, fault process, or historical anomaly, the outage cannot be confirmed from live evidence. The current network state is fully healthy.
=== END ===